<div class="container prose">
  <p>A running toilet can waste hundreds of gallons a week—expensive on a Houston water bill. Weak flushes often trace to clogged rim jets from mineral buildup or failing fill valves. We stock common repair parts and can swap an aging toilet when repairs would only buy a short reprieve.</p>
  <h2>Signs you need service</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Phantom refills or continuous hissing</li>
    <li>Rocking bowl or water at the base (wax seal concern)</li>
    <li>Cracks in the tank or bowl</li>
    <li>Frequent double-flushing still leaves waste behind</li>
  </ul>
